===persian===

شهر دود
شهر داد

شهر بی داد

شهر نیش

شهر نوش
شهر شب گرفته خاموش
در شهر دود
کودکی را دیدم
نامش رستم بود
خسته و سوار بر اسب چوبین شکسته
می خواند
من میترسم... می ترسم... می ترسم
چوب گزینم کو...
و مادرش صدا میزد
های رستم درست را بخوان
رستم درس خواند
رستم مرد شد...
و از اسب چوبینش میزی ساختند.

تهران ۱۳۴۰

===machine===

City of Smoke
City of Dad
City of Nod
City of Nish
City of Drink
City of Silence in the Night
In the City of Smoke
I saw a child
His name was Rostam
Tired and riding a broken wooden horse
He was singing
I am afraid... I am afraid... I am afraid
I will choose a stick...
And his mother was calling
Hey Rostam, sing the right song
Rostam studied
Rostam became a man...
And they made a table out of his wooden horse.

Tehran 1961

===lantern===

City of smoke,
city of justice,
city of injustice,
city of the sting,
city of the sweet draught,
city gone silent, taken by night.
In the city of smoke
I saw a child
whose name was Rostam,
tired, astride a broken wooden horse,
and he was singing:
I'm afraid... afraid... afraid...
where is my whittled stick...?
And his mother kept calling,
Rostam, sing it right —
so Rostam learned his lesson,
Rostam became a man...
and out of his wooden horse they built a desk.

Tehran, 1340

